***

The present invention relates to a method (METH) for measuring a distance $R$ between a vehicle (V) and an identifier (I) used for vehicle access and engine start, wherein the vehicle (V) and the identifier (I) are synchronized. 

The method (METH) comprises the following steps:

*   **Selecting** ($\text{Sel\_f}_p$) $N$ frequencies $f_p$, where $p \in [1, N]$ and $N$ is a natural number greater than 3;
*   **Executing** $N$ sequences $Sq_p$, each sequence $Sq_p$ comprising the following sub-steps:
    *   **Transmitting** ($\text{Em\_Sv}_p$) a first signal ($Sv_p$) of frequency $f_p$ from a transmitter ($\text{TX}_v$) of the vehicle (V) to a receiver ($\text{RX}_i$) of the identifier (I);
    *   **Measuring** ($\text{Mes\_}\varphi_{vip}$), using a computing unit ($X_i$) of the identifier (I), a modulo $2\pi$ phase $\varphi_{vip}$ of the received first signal ($Sv_p$) relative to a second signal ($Si_p$) with a phase defined by $\varphi_{ip}(t) = \varphi_{0ip} + 2\pi f_p t$;
    *   **Transmitting** ($\text{Em\_Si}_p$) the second signal ($Si_p$) from a transmitter ($\text{TX}_i$) of the identifier (I) to a receiver ($\text{RX}_v$) of the vehicle (V);
    *   **Calculating** ($\text{Mes\_}\varphi_{ivp}$), using a computing unit ($X_v$) of the vehicle (V), a modulo $2\pi$ phase $\varphi_{ivp}$ of the received second signal ($Si_p$) relative to the first signal ($Sv_p$);
    *   **Calculating** ($\text{Cal\_}\varphi_p$) the average phase $\varphi_p$ of the phases $\varphi_{vip}$ and $\varphi_{ivp}$;
*   **Calculating** ($\text{Cal\_P}_p$), for each $p$ from $1$ to $N-1$, a phase slope $P_p$ using the formula: 
    $$P_p = \frac{\varphi_{p+1} - \varphi_p}{f_{p+1} - f_p}$$
*   **Calculating** ($\text{Cal\_R}$) the distance $R$ from the phase slopes $P_p$, for $p \in [1, N]$.

